{
  "_comment": "Clayworks Bench SCENE DEFINITION (201F4F51 template-free). The asset-pipeline editor: a wizard over three LINEAR workflow definitions (params.workflows — branching lives BETWEEN definitions, chosen by the Task cards), a 2×2 editor viewport (the `editor_quad` rtt — the behaviour tiles its QuadGrid inside the reserved rect), a floating right inspector whose per-stage cells gate on the step surfaces (`wf_step_<id>`) and the conform ROLE flags (`on_conform_*`), a display-toggle panel over the viewport, and the Back/Next footer that drives the rail. The `assetpipeline` behaviour plays it (flicker-assetpipeline); assetpipeline.lua derives the rail-chip styles and the bank-row selection washes. Styles: the live blocks folded in from the crate's quarantined scene_styles.json (col/map/panel/well/seam/checkbox/rowsel/card); the dead template-era blocks (window/frame/option_grid/layout/header/tab_bar/footer dims) did not move.",
  "behaviour": "assetpipeline",
  "params": {
    "_comment": "Workflow DEFINITIONS for the bench's vendored Workflow runtime: `workflows.<name>` is one LINEAR wizard — the ordered `steps` ({ id, title, needs, yields }). Branching is deliberately absent (Aaron, ratified 2026-08-01): a required branch is a SEPARATE definition, chosen up front by the Task cards — Character (and the unclassified default) walks import_character, Prop/Accessory import_prop, Animation import_animation, so the old in-spine 'skip Attach for a non-character' conditional is simply a definition without the step. `needs`/`yields` name keys of the bench's per-frame step DOCUMENT (a key is present exactly when the scene state it names exists — `wf_doc`): `source` = an open scanned folder, `class` = the declared AssetClass, `rig` = the character conform produced its Rig, `attach` = the authored attach-point set, `fit` = the prop/garment mount binding applies, `clip` = the active BVH retargeted onto the reference skeleton, `committed` = the baked rig / emitted clip path. `Next` into a step whose needs are unmet refuses, fail-loud. Step `title` is the rail-chip label, a `$token` resolved through the stringtable at publish.",
    "workflows": {
      "import_character": {
        "title": "$ap_character",
        "steps": [
          { "id": "task", "title": "$wf_step_task", "yields": ["source", "class"] },
          { "id": "conform", "title": "$wf_step_rig", "needs": ["source"], "yields": ["rig"] },
          { "id": "attach", "title": "$wf_step_attach", "needs": ["rig"], "yields": ["attach"] },
          { "id": "review", "title": "$wf_step_review", "needs": ["rig", "attach"], "yields": ["committed"] }
        ]
      },
      "import_prop": {
        "title": "$ap_prop",
        "steps": [
          { "id": "task", "title": "$wf_step_task", "yields": ["source", "class"] },
          { "id": "conform", "title": "$wf_step_mount", "needs": ["source"], "yields": ["fit"] },
          { "id": "review", "title": "$wf_step_review", "needs": ["fit"], "yields": ["committed"] }
        ]
      },
      "import_animation": {
        "title": "$ap_animation",
        "steps": [
          { "id": "task", "title": "$wf_step_task", "yields": ["source", "class"] },
          { "id": "conform", "title": "$wf_step_clip", "needs": ["source"], "yields": ["clip"] },
          { "id": "review", "title": "$wf_step_review", "needs": ["clip"], "yields": ["committed"] }
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "styles": {
    "window": {
      "_comment": "This bench's root slab — scene-owned like every migrated bench's (a shared file would fork the look; duplication is the pattern). Only draw-read keys.",
      "radius": 4,
      "fill_top": "$stone3",
      "fill_bot": "$stone1",
      "border": "$edge2",
      "shadow": "$shadow",
      "shadow_dy": 18,
      "shadow_feather": 46,
      "shadow_grow": 4
    },
    "workflow": {
      "_comment": "The step-rail chip trio the vendored Workflow runtime's states resolve to: the pair script derives `wf_<id>_style` = workflow.chip.<state> from the published `wf_<id>_state` (active / visited / todo).",
      "chip": {
        "active": {
          "fill_top": "$sap_base",
          "fill_bot": "$sap_base_lo",
          "border": "$sap_border",
          "border_w": 1,
          "label": "$ink_bright",
          "radius": 3
        },
        "visited": {
          "fill_top": "$stone3",
          "fill_bot": "$stone2",
          "border": "$edge2",
          "border_w": 1,
          "label": "$bronze",
          "radius": 3
        },
        "todo": {
          "fill_top": "$stone2",
          "fill_bot": "$stone1",
          "border": "$edge1",
          "border_w": 1,
          "label": "$dim",
          "radius": 3
        }
      }
    },
    "assetpipeline": {
      "col": {
        "ink": "$ink_bright",
        "ink_dim": "$ink",
        "dim": "$dim",
        "faint": "$faint",
        "bronze": "$bronze",
        "rail": "$dim_soft",
        "sapphire": "$sapphire"
      },
      "_map_comment": "BONE-MAP / REQUIREMENT COLOUR KEY — the one place the conform provenance states get their colour. ok = a source bone renamed to canonical; review = placed by a derive pass (hip/shoulder/ankle) and worth a human's eye; auto = inferred from the reference rig; fail = a Review requirement that is not met. Bound per-row as a dotted path via `<row>_color`, so the key cannot drift between the list and the summary.",
      "map": {
        "ok": "$sig_green",
        "review": "$sig_yellow",
        "auto": "$sig_blue",
        "fail": "$hp_hi"
      },
      "panel": {
        "fill_top": "$stone3",
        "fill_bot": "$stone1",
        "border": "$edge2",
        "border_w": 1,
        "radius": 4,
        "focused": {
          "fill_top": "$stone4",
          "fill_bot": "$stone2",
          "border": "$sap_border",
          "border_w": 1,
          "radius": 4
        }
      },
      "well": {
        "fill_top": "$well_top",
        "fill_bot": "$well_bot",
        "border": "$edge1",
        "border_w": 1,
        "radius": 3
      },
      "seam": {
        "fill_top": "$seam",
        "fill_bot": "$seam"
      },
      "holder": {
        "fill_top": [0, 0, 0, 0],
        "fill_bot": [0, 0, 0, 0],
        "border": "$bronze_deep",
        "border_w": 1,
        "radius": 3
      },
      "checkbox": {
        "box": "$stone2",
        "check": "$sig_green",
        "border": "$edge4",
        "pad": 3
      },
      "slider": {
        "track": "$well",
        "border": "$edge2",
        "fill": "$sap_base",
        "fill_hi": "$sap_border",
        "handle": "$sap_border",
        "handle_w": 14
      },
      "button": {
        "fill_top": "$stone4",
        "fill_bot": "$stone2",
        "border": "$edge3",
        "border_w": 1,
        "radius": 3
      },
      "bar": {
        "fill_top": "$stone4",
        "fill_bot": "$stone3",
        "border": "$edge2",
        "border_w": 1,
        "radius": 3
      },
      "_rowsel_comment": "The bank rows' LIST-SELECTION washes: the pair script derives each row's `style_bind` path from the published sel/window numbers — the selected slot wears `rowsel` (the sapphire accent wash), the rest `rowsel_off` (draws next to nothing under the bound label).",
      "rowsel": {
        "fill_top": "$accent_wash_2",
        "fill_bot": "$accent_wash",
        "hover_top": "$accent_wash_2",
        "hover_bot": "$accent_wash_2",
        "border": "$sapphire",
        "border_w": 1,
        "radius": 2,
        "label": "$ink"
      },
      "rowsel_off": {
        "fill_top": "$stage_void",
        "fill_bot": "$stage_void",
        "hover_top": "$accent_wash",
        "hover_bot": "$accent_wash",
        "radius": 2,
        "label": "$ink"
      },
      "card": {
        "fill_top": "$stage_void",
        "fill_bot": "$stage_void",
        "hover_top": "$accent_wash",
        "hover_bot": "$accent_wash",
        "border": "$edge3",
        "hover_border": "$sapphire",
        "border_w": 1,
        "radius": 3,
        "glow": "$sap_glow",
        "label": "$ink_bright",
        "hover_label": "$ink_bright"
      }
    }
  },
